es. </li> <li>Demonstrated interest in generative AI and productivity tooling (e.g., ChatGPT, Copilot, n8n, Zapier, Replit Code Agent, etc…).</li> <li>Familiarity with a wide range of functional AI use cases—marketing, operations, finance, education, etc.</li> <li>Experience in curriculum development, instructional design, or education technology.</li> <li>Excellent written and verbal communication skills.</li> <li>Ability to work cross-functionally with content creators, educators, and subject matter experts.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Why Datacamp? </strong></p> <p>Joining DataCamp means becoming part of a dynamic, creative, and international start-up. Here are just a few of the reasons why you’ll love being on our team:</p> <ul> <li> <strong>Exciting Challenges</strong> – Tackle some of the most important educational challenges in AI.</li> <li> <strong>Work with the Best Instructors</strong> – Partner with top-tier instructors from leading organizations like Microsoft, Hugging Face, AWS, and more.</li> <li> <strong>Competitive Compensation</strong> – We offer a competitive salary with attractive benefits.</li> <li> <strong>Work Flexibility</strong> – Benefit from flexible working hours and a remote-friendly culture.</li> <li> <strong>Professional Growth</strong> – Access to a yearly learning &amp; development budget.</li> <li> <strong>Global Culture</strong> – Join a team that values international collaboration and retreats.</li> <li> <strong>Tools &amp; Setup</strong> – Receive an annual IT equipment budget to refresh your workspace.</li> </ul> <p>Our competitive compensation package offers additional benefits. On top of your salary you will also receive extra legal benefits such as best-in-class medical insurance including dental and vision. Depending on your location additional benefits might be available to you.</p> <p>At DataCamp, we value diverse experiences and perspectives. If you’re excited about this role but don\'t meet every qualification, we still encourage you to apply. We believe skills can be developed and are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can thrive. Your unique talents and perspectives are what make our team great!</p> ','https://jobs.techstars.com/companies/datacamp/jobs/50967973-curriculum-manager-in-artificial-intelligence#content','startups\ncorporations\ncommunities\ninvestors\nmission','https://cdn.getro.com/companies/5e2df1f9-1a95-5675-a0ee-60f30af3fa42-1748655610','DataCamp','https://boards.greenhouse.io/datacamp/jobs/6885254?utm_source=Techstars+job+board&utm_medium=getro.com&gh_src=Techstars+job+board','Curriculum Manager in Artificial Intelligence'),(132,1747267200,'<p><strong>About DataCamp</strong></p> <p>DataCamp\'s mission is to empower everyone with the data and AI skills essential for 21st-century success. By providing practical, engaging learning experiences, DataCamp equips learners and organizations of all sizes to harness the power of data and AI. As a trusted partner to over 14 million learners and 5,000+ companies, including 80% of the Fortune 1000, DataCamp is leading the charge in addressing the critical data and AI skills shortage.</p> <p><strong>About the role</strong></p> <p>Large Language Models, agentic systems, and new developer tooling are fundamentally transforming the software development landscape—and the demand for skilled AI engineers has never been greater. As an <strong>AI Engineering Curriculum Manager</strong>, you’ll be at the forefront of building world-class technical content that helps train current and aspiring software developers and data scientists.</p> <p>You will work closely with a team of expert instructors and cross-functional stakeholders across curriculum, engineering, and product to create hands-on learning experiences that teach AI engineering skills. This includes content on building AI systems (RAG, fine-tuning, etc…), prompt engineering, system design for AI applications, and leveraging modern frameworks and toolchains (like LangChain, Hugging Face, Vector DBs, and more).</p> <p>You’ll play a pivotal role in developing a curriculum at the intersection of software engineering and AI, driving our mission to democratize advanced AI education.</p> <p><strong>About you</strong></p> <p>At DataCamp, we value action, ownership, transparency, and a deep focus on learners. You’re someone who:</p> <ul> <li>Has a strong technical background and can navigate the full AI stack—from using the latest models to setting up guardrails.</li> <li>Stays current with the latest trends, tools, and techniques shaping the AI engineering ecosystem. You have a deep passion for this space.</li> <li>Is passionate about education and wants to shape how the next generation of AI engineers learn.</li> <li>Thrives in fast-paced environments and brings structure to ambiguity.</li> <li>Communicates clearly and can distill complex concepts into intuitive learning experiences.</li> </ul> <p>If that sounds like you, we’d love to meet you.</p> <p><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p> <p>In this role, you will focus your time on the following areas:</p> <p>Content Creation &amp; Strategy</p> <ul> <li>Design and develop a curriculum covering technical AI engineering topics, such as:</li> <ul> <li>Building and deploying AI systems (e.g., RAG, fine-tuning, etc…).</li> <li>Building agentic applications using frameworks like LangChain, CrewAI, smolagents, and more.</li> <li>Prompt engineering and evaluation, focusing on reliability, reproducibility, and performance.</li> <li>System design and architecture for scalable, real-world AI applications.</li> <li>Tooling and infrastructure, including vector databases, orchestration tools, and cloud-native deployment strategies.</li> </ul> <li>Collaborate with instructors to create engaging learning materials.</li> <li>Be learner zero, and act as the voice of the learner. You will review code, exercises, and course material to ensure technical accuracy and pedagogy.</li> <li>Continuously assess content performance using learner feedback and engagement data (via Looker and SQL) to drive improvements.</li> <li>Identify and prioritize high-impact AI engineering topics for new content development.</li> <li>Source and recruit top-tier instructors with deep expertise in relevant tools, frameworks, and methodologies.</li> </ul> <p>Project Management &amp; Collaboration</p> <ul> <li>Own the end-to-end content development lifecycle for new courses.</li> <li>Set project timelines and manage instructor contributions.</li> <li>Coordinate with subject matter experts to scope and validate content.</li> <li>Champion content excellence through internal reviews and structured feedback loops.</li> <li>Identify ways AI can streamline content production processes and improve content quality.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Qualifications</strong></p> <ul> <li>Strong software engineering background, with experience in:</li> <ul> <li>Python, APIs, cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, or Azure).</li> <li>Working with LLMs and developer toolchains for AI apps (e.g., LangChain, Hugging Face Transformers, LlamaIndex, vector databases, etc…).</li> <li>Building and deploying AI-powered applications or tools.</li> </ul> <li>Experience with prompt engineering in a production environment, model evaluation, or fine-tuning is a major plus.</li> <li>Experience in a technical education role or content creation is highly preferred.</li> <li>Strong written communication skills and attention to detail.</li> <li>Ability to work collaboratively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Why Datacamp? </strong></p> <p>Joining DataCamp means becoming part of a dynamic, creative, and international start-up. Here are just a few of the reasons why you’ll love being on our team:</p> <ul> <li> <strong>Exciting Challenges</strong> – Tackle some of the most important educational challenges in AI.</li> <li> <strong>Work with the Best Instructors</strong> – Partner with top-tier instructors from leading organizations like Microsoft, Hugging Face, AWS, and more.</li> <li> <strong>Competitive Compensation</strong> – We offer a competitive salary with attractive benefits.</li> <li> <strong>Work Flexibility</strong> – Benefit from flexible working hours and a remote-friendly culture.</li> <li> <strong>Professional Growth</strong> – Access to a yearly learning &amp; development budget.</li> <li> <strong>Global Culture</strong> – Join a team that values international collaboration and retreats.</li> <li> <strong>Tools &amp; Setup</strong> – Receive an annual IT equipment budget to refresh your workspace.</li> </ul> <p>Our competitive compensation package offers additional benefits. On top of your salary you will also receive extra legal benefits such as best-in-class medical insurance including dental and vision. Depending on your location additional benefits might be available to you.</p> <p>At DataCamp, we value diverse experiences and perspectives. If you’re excited about this role but don\'t meet every qualification, we still encourage you to apply. We believe skills can be developed and are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can thrive. Your unique talents and perspectives are what make our team great!</p>','https://jobs.techstars.com/companies/datacamp/jobs/50967969-ai-engineering-curriculum-manager#content','startups\ncorporations\ncommunities\ninvestors\nmission','https://cdn.getro.com/companies/5e2df1f9-1a95-5675-a0ee-60f30af3fa42-1748655610','DataCamp','https://boards.greenhouse.io/datacamp/jobs/6885014?utm_source=Techstars+job+board&utm_medium=getro.com&gh_src=Techstars+job+board','AI Engineering Curriculum Manager'),(133,1747267200,' <p><strong>About DataCamp</strong></p> <p>DataCamp\'s mission is to empower everyone with the data and AI skills essential for 21st-century success. By providing practical, engaging learning experiences, DataCamp equips learners and organizations of all sizes to harness the power of data and AI. As a trusted partner to over 14 million learners and 5,000+ companies, including 80% of the Fortune 1000, DataCamp is leading the charge in addressing the critical data and AI skills shortage.</p> <p><strong>About the role</strong></p> <p>The rapid rise of generative AI is transforming how work gets done across every function—from marketing and finance to HR, product, and customer service. Yet, most professionals lack the foundational knowledge and practical confidence to use AI effectively and responsibly.</p> <p>As <strong>Curriculum Manager in Artificial Intelligence</strong>, you’ll lead the development of a best-in-class curriculum that bridges the gap between conceptual understanding and practical application. Your focus will be on building AI courses for professionals across diverse domains.</p> <p>You’ll work with expert instructors, curriculum designers, and cross-functional teams to create interactive learning experiences that help professionals understand how AI works, what it can and can’t do, and how to use it to augment their day-to-day work using the latest tools and workflows.</p> <p>This role is ideal for someone passionate about making AI accessible, impactful, and intuitive for everyone, regardless of technical background.</p> <p><strong>About you</strong></p> <p>At DataCamp, we value initiative, clarity, ownership, and a learner-first mindset. You’re someone who:</p> <ul> <li>Understands the broader implications of AI across industries and job functions.</li> <li>Has a solid technical foundation and a genuine understanding of how AI tools work—you don’t just use them at face value or rely on hype.</li> <li>Can empathize with and build educational content for different profiles, from leaders to front-line workers and everyone in between. </li> <li>Is deeply curious about AI tools, trends, and applications—especially in applied settings.</li> <li>Stays current with the latest trends, tools, and techniques shaping the AI ecosystem.</li> <li>Thrives on collaboration, thrives in ambiguity, and takes ownership from idea to launch.</li> <li>Communicates clearly and enjoys translating abstract concepts into actionable insight.</li> </ul> <p>If that resonates with you, we’d love to hear from you.</p> <p><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p> <p>In this role, you will focus your time on the following areas:</p> <p>Content Strategy &amp; Development</p> <ul> <li>Design and manage a curriculum focused on AI concepts and off-the-shelf tooling, including:</li> <ul> <li>Conceptual foundations of AI and machine learning (e.g., how generative models work, responsible AI best practices, what AI agents are, etc…).</li> <li>Content around AI workflows, best practices, and limitations tailored to specific business functions (e.g., marketing, customer support, HR, finance, education, and product management)</li> <li>Tools beyond ChatGPT—extending to function-specific assistants and tools (e.g., GitHub Copilot, Windsurf, n8n, Zapier, Perplexity, etc.)</li> <li>Prompt writing, task design, and evaluation techniques tailored to business users.</li> </ul> <li>Collaborate with instructors to create accessible, engaging, and high-impact learning experiences.</li> <li>Act as learner zero—ensuring all content is intuitive, actionable, and aligned with learner needs.</li> <li>Use learner feedback, content analytics (via Looker and SQL), and industry signals to improve existing content and inform new course development.</li> <li>Source and recruit top-tier instructors with deep expertise in relevant tools, frameworks, and methodologies.</li> </ul> <p>Project Management &amp; Collaboration</p> <ul> <li>Own the end-to-end content development lifecycle for new courses.</li> <li>Set project timelines and manage instructor contributions.</li> <li>Coordinate with subject matter experts to scope and validate content.</li> <li>Champion content excellence through internal reviews and structured feedback loops.</li> <li>Identify ways AI can streamline content production processes and improve content quality.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Qualifications</strong></p> <ul> <li>Strong technical background, focusing on clearly communicating concepts to non-technical audiences. </li> <li>Demonstrated interest in generative AI and productivity tooling (e.g., ChatGPT, Copilot, n8n, Zapier, Replit Code Agent, etc…).</li> <li>Familiarity with a wide range of functional AI use cases—marketing, operations, finance, education, etc.</li> <li>Experience in curriculum development, instructional design, or education technology.</li> <li>Excellent written and verbal communication skills.</li> <li>Ability to work cross-functionally with content creators, educators, and subject matter experts.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Why Datacamp? </strong></p> <p>Joining DataCamp means becoming part of a dynamic, creative, and international start-up. Here are just a few of the reasons why you’ll love being on our team:</p> <ul> <li> <strong>Exciting Challenges</strong> – Tackle some of the most important educational challenges in AI.</li> <li> <strong>Work with the Best Instructors</strong> – Partner with top-tier instructors from leading organizations like Microsoft, Hugging Face, AWS, and more.</li> <li> <strong>Competitive Compensation</strong> – We offer a competitive salary with attractive benefits.</li> <li> <strong>Work Flexibility</strong> – Benefit from flexible working hours and a remote-friendly culture.</li> <li> <strong>Professional Growth</strong> – Access to a yearly learning &amp; development budget.</li> <li> <strong>Global Culture</strong> – Join a team that values international collaboration and retreats.</li> <li> <strong>Tools &amp; Setup</strong> – Receive an annual IT equipment budget to refresh your workspace.</li> </ul> <p>Our competitive compensation package offers additional benefits. On top of your salary you will also receive extra legal benefits such as best-in-class medical insurance including dental and vision. Depending on your location additional benefits might be available to you.</p> <p>At DataCamp, we value diverse experiences and perspectives. If you’re excited about this role but don\'t meet every qualification, we still encourage you to apply. We believe skills can be developed and are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can thrive. Your unique talents and perspectives are what make our team great!</p> ','https://jobs.techstars.com/companies/datacamp/jobs/50967972-curriculum-manager-in-artificial-intelligence#content','startups\ncorporations\ncommunities\ninvestors\nmission','https://cdn.getro.com/companies/5e2df1f9-1a95-5675-a0ee-60f30af3fa42-1748655610','DataCamp','https://boards.greenhouse.io/datacamp/jobs/6885253?utm_source=Techstars+job+board&utm_medium=getro.com&gh_src=Techstars+job+board','Curriculum Manager in Artificial Intelligence'),(134,1747267200,' <p><strong>About DataCamp</strong></p> <p>DataCamp\'s mission is to empower everyone with the data and AI skills essential for 21st-century success. By providing practical, engaging learning experiences, DataCamp equips learners and organizations of all sizes to harness the power of data and AI. As a trusted partner to over 14 million learners and 5,000+ companies, including 80% of the Fortune 1000, DataCamp is leading the charge in addressing the critical data and AI skills shortage.</p> <p><strong>About the role</strong></p> <p>Large Language Models, agentic systems, and new developer tooling are fundamentally transforming the software development landscape—and the demand for skilled AI engineers has never been greater. As an <strong>AI Engineering Curriculum Manager</strong>, you’ll be at the forefront of building world-class technical content that helps train current and aspiring software developers and data scientists.</p> <p>You will work closely with a team of expert instructors and cross-functional stakeholders across curriculum, engineering, and product to create hands-on learning experiences that teach AI engineering skills. This includes content on building AI systems (RAG, fine-tuning, etc…), prompt engineering, system design for AI applications, and leveraging modern frameworks and toolchains (like LangChain, Hugging Face, Vector DBs, and more).</p> <p>You’ll play a pivotal role in developing a curriculum at the intersection of software engineering and AI, driving our mission to democratize advanced AI education.</p> <p><strong>About you</strong></p> <p>At DataCamp, we value action, ownership, transparency, and a deep focus on learners. You’re someone who:</p> <ul> <li>Has a strong technical background and can navigate the full AI stack—from using the latest models to setting up guardrails.</li> <li>Stays current with the latest trends, tools, and techniques shaping the AI engineering ecosystem. You have a deep passion for this space.</li> <li>Is passionate about education and wants to shape how the next generation of AI engineers learn.</li> <li>Thrives in fast-paced environments and brings structure to ambiguity.</li> <li>Communicates clearly and can distill complex concepts into intuitive learning experiences.</li> </ul> <p>If that sounds like you, we’d love to meet you.</p> <p><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p> <p>In this role, you will focus your time on the following areas:</p> <p>Content Creation &amp; Strategy</p> <ul> <li>Design and develop a curriculum covering technical AI engineering topics, such as:</li> <ul> <li>Building and deploying AI systems (e.g., RAG, fine-tuning, etc…).</li> <li>Building agentic applications using frameworks like LangChain, CrewAI, smolagents, and more.</li> <li>Prompt engineering and evaluation, focusing on reliability, reproducibility, and performance.</li> <li>System design and architecture for scalable, real-world AI applications.</li> <li>Tooling and infrastructure, including vector databases, orchestration tools, and cloud-native deployment strategies.</li> </ul> <li>Collaborate with instructors to create engaging learning materials.</li> <li>Be learner zero, and act as the voice of the learner. You will review code, exercises, and course material to ensure technical accuracy and pedagogy.</li> <li>Continuously assess content performance using learner feedback and engagement data (via Looker and SQL) to drive improvements.</li> <li>Identify and prioritize high-impact AI engineering topics for new content development.</li> <li>Source and recruit top-tier instructors with deep expertise in relevant tools, frameworks, and methodologies.</li> </ul> <p>Project Management &amp; Collaboration</p> <ul> <li>Own the end-to-end content development lifecycle for new courses.</li> <li>Set project timelines and manage instructor contributions.</li> <li>Coordinate with subject matter experts to scope and validate content.</li> <li>Champion content excellence through internal reviews and structured feedback loops.</li> <li>Identify ways AI can streamline content production processes and improve content quality.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Qualifications</strong></p> <ul> <li>Strong software engineering background, with experience in:</li> <ul> <li>Python, APIs, cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, or Azure).</li> <li>Working with LLMs and developer toolchains for AI apps (e.g., LangChain, Hugging Face Transformers, LlamaIndex, vector databases, etc…).</li> <li>Building and deploying AI-powered applications or tools.</li> </ul> <li>Experience with prompt engineering in a production environment, model evaluation, or fine-tuning is a major plus.</li> <li>Experience in a technical education role or content creation is highly preferred.</li> <li>Strong written communication skills and attention to detail.</li> <li>Ability to work collaboratively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Why Datacamp? </strong></p> <p>Joining DataCamp means becoming part of a dynamic, creative, and international start-up. Here are just a few of the reasons why you’ll love being on our team:</p> <ul> <li> <strong>Exciting Challenges</strong> – Tackle some of the most important educational challenges in AI.</li> <li> <strong>Work with the Best Instructors</strong> – Partner with top-tier instructors from leading organizations like Microsoft, Hugging Face, AWS, and more.</li> <li> <strong>Competitive Compensation</strong> – We offer a competitive salary with attractive benefits.</li> <li> <strong>Work Flexibility</strong> – Benefit from flexible working hours and a remote-friendly culture.</li> <li> <strong>Professional Growth</strong> – Access to a yearly learning &amp; development budget.</li> <li> <strong>Global Culture</strong> – Join a team that values international collaboration and retreats.</li> <li> <strong>Tools &amp; Setup</strong> – Receive an annual IT equipment budget to refresh your workspace.</li> </ul>  <p>Our competitive compensation package offers additional benefits. Part of your salary can be allocated to a company car or mobility budget, on top of your salary you will also receive extra-legal benefits such as Equity, the best in class medical insurance including dental and vision, Group insurance (pension, invalidity, and life), monthly net allowances based on your role, meal vouchers, eco vouchers, lunch is ordered for you whenever you work from the office, Bike km allowance if you cycle to work and 20 paid holidays with the option to buy more. </p> <p>At DataCamp, we value diverse experiences and perspectives. If you’re excited about this role but don\'t meet every qualification, we still encourage you to apply. We believe skills can be developed and are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can thrive. Your unique talents and perspectives are what make our team great!</p> <p> </p>','https://jobs.techstars.com/companies/datacamp/jobs/50967964-ai-engineering-curriculum-manager#content','startups\ncorporations\ncommunities\ninvestors\nmission','https://cdn.getro.com/companies/5e2d