 resolve issues related to system performance, network configurations, and server uptime.</li> <li>Implement monitoring, alerting, and logging solutions to ensure the reliability and health of production systems.</li> <li>Ensure infrastructure is secure, compliant, and aligned with industry best practices.</li> <li>Develop and maintain disaster recovery plans, backups, and redundancy measures to minimize downtime.</li> <li>Optimize development and deployment workflows to improve efficiency and reduce manual intervention.</li> <li>Participate in on-call rotations to support the operational needs of the production environment.</li> <li>Stay up-to-date with industry trends and emerging technologies to continuously improve our DevOps practices.</li> <li>Contribute to team success by supporting the broader goals of the engineering department and the company.</li> </ul> <h3>Requirements ✔️</h3> <ul> <li>2+ years of experience in DevOps, system administration, or cloud engineering (or equivalent expertise with ~5000 hours of deliberate practice).</li> <li>Expertise in cloud platforms (CPG Preferred), including provisioning and managing resources, as well as optimizing cost and performance.</li> <li>Experience with containerization tools (Docker, Kubernetes) for building, deploying, and scaling applications.</li> <li>Strong understanding of infrastructure automation.</li> <li>Familiarity with CI/CD tools to automate deployment pipelines (GitHub actions preferred).</li> <li>Proficient in scripting and automation (Bash and Python) for infrastructure and system management.</li> <li>Strong understanding of network configurations, firewalls, load balancers, and DNS management.</li> <li>Experience implementing monitoring, alerting, and logging systems (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, ELK stack).</li> <li>Knowledge of security practices related to cloud infrastructure, including IAM, encryption, and compliance.</li> <li>Strong problem-solving, debugging, and performance optimization skills.</li> <li>Excellent communication skills (Spanish, and English).</li> <li>Ability to work independently and remotely in a fast-paced environment.</li> </ul> <h3>Benefits ✔️<br><br>At AltScore, we believe in providing our team members with a comprehensive benefits package that supports their overall health and wellbeing. We offer the following compensation package to eligible employees:</h3> <ul> <li> <strong>Base Salary:</strong> $2,000 - $8,000 USD per month, depending on skills according to our engineering scale L3 - L6.</li> <li> <strong>Performance Bonus:</strong> Based on achievement of agreed KPIs.</li> <li> <strong>Unlimited PTO</strong> (with an expectation of taking at least 3-4 weeks per year off) We understand that maintaining a healthy work-life balance is crucial for long-term productivity and wellbeing.</li> <li> <strong>Employee stock ownership plan</strong> (ESOP) - Every single employee gets an ESOP. At AltScore, we believe that every member of the company should feel like a partner from day 1.</li> <li> <strong>Remote:</strong> At AltScore, we are a fully remote company, and we encourage employees to work from wherever they are most comfortable and productive. Employees must work in the Americas timezone.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div>','https://jobs.techstars.com/companies/altscore-2/jobs/50614164-devops-engineer#content','startups\ncorporations\ncommunities\ninvestors\nmission','https://cdn.getro.com/companies/6a5adf7a-cb52-5683-aa26-dd0f364a1790-1747964103','AltScore','https://boards.greenhouse.io/altscore/jobs/4492961008?utm_source=Techstars+job+board&utm_medium=getro.com&gh_src=Techstars+job+board','Devops Engineer'),(165,1746748800,'<div> <div> <div> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <p><strong>We are in search of a highly skilled and motivated DevOps Engineer to join our growing team.</strong> In this role, you will work closely with the CTO and engineering teams to design, implement, and mai